1. e4
{ Ian Shahic (White) opens with pawn to e4. This is the Croatian Grand Chester, penultimate round, featuring Croatia's number one player against world champion Gukesh Dommaraju. }
1... e5 { Gukesh responds with e5. The Ruy Lopez is coming. } 2. Nf3
{ Knight to f3 by White. } 2... Nc6 { Knight to c6 by Black. } 3. Bb5
{ Bishop to b5 - the Ruy Lopez (Spanish Opening) is on the board. } 3... a6
{ Morphy's defense with a6. } 4. Ba4
{ Bishop to a4. Capablanca famously refuted the Marshall attack over the board in New York 1918 against Frank Marshall, but unless you are the next Capablanca, you are not refuting it over the board. }
4... Nf6 { Knight to f6. } 5. O-O { Castles kingside by White. } 5... Be7
{ Bishop to e7 by Black. } 6. Re1 { Rook to e1 by White. } 6... b5
