Nxd5 { Knight captures on d5. } 10. Nxe5 { Knight captures on e5 by White. }
10... Nxe5 { Knight captures back. } 11. Rxe5
{ Rook captures on e5. White is up a pawn - this is the standard Marshall attack position. In the original game, Frank James Marshall played Nf6 against Capablanca, which can still be played, but Nc6 was found to be much stronger. }
11... Bb7
{ Bishop to b7 - the third most popular reply and almost no one plays it. However, Magnus Carlson played it, Levon Aronian played it quite a few times with very nice results, and Arjun Erigaisi also played it. You have to be ready for it even though there are far fewer games in the database than with Nf6 or c6. }
12. d4
{ Pawn to d4. Playing d4 right away is not considered the best for White. } (
12. Qf3
