14. Qe3
{ Queen to e3 - you might think: can't we just play Qe3? We're up a piece, offering to trade queens. If Black captures, we give up a rook for two pieces. But White is actually dead lost here if Black finds the only winning move. }
14... Rae8
{ Rook a to e8 is the ONLY winning move! Why? You still can't move the queen because you're getting checkmated. If you trade queens it seems OK but Rfd8 still leads to checkmate. White cannot play f3 because of check on e1 and e2, and the bishop covers g3. White must play f4 but then the bishop on c1 is hanging. Even after Re1+, Kf2, BxD5, capturing the rook, BxD5, RxC1 - White is still lost because there's no defense against the other rook coming to e1, then the knight falls, and White is out of moves. }
15. Qxe7
{ Queen trade variation - but as shown, Black can avoid this with Rae8 and maintain a winning attack. }
) ( 13. Bxd5
